{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"865236c05b2a2bab","type":"text","text":"# Grave Butterflies\n\nA grave is covered with small black pebbles. A butterfly sits on the stones. It looks as if it is there to die, and turn into a pebble itself.\n\n![Grave Butterflies](2026-06-02-grave-butterfly.jpeg)","x":-460,"y":200,"width":380,"height":830},
		{"id":"9dd1f0836702ae0f","type":"text","text":"# Portal Trees\n\nDuring my first meeting with Sandrine and Verena, the gardeners at the Cemetery of Kings, Verena told me about the myth surrounding the Cedars, which, in some beliefs, represent a gateway between the world of the living and the world of the dead.\n\n![Portal Trees](2026-06-02-portal-tree.jpeg)\n","x":780,"y":980,"width":380,"height":911},
		{"id":"f01a802c7ce04d08","type":"text","text":"# Trimming the ivy\n\nSandrine and Verena are trimming the ivy at the base of the tree trunk. This is both for aesthetic reasons and to allow the tree to breathe.\n\n![Trimming the ivy](2026-06-02-trimming-the-ivy.jpeg)","x":-400,"y":1180,"width":380,"height":815},
		{"id":"918ccc9fb9741241","type":"text","text":"# Rare Moss\n\nRare types of moss grow on graves. A form of new life, a new ecosystem born from the dead. These mosses are protected. Graves are not allowed to be cleaned (except by families). These rare mosses grow because the material of the graves is not native.\n\n![](2026-06-02-rare-moss.jpeg)","x":220,"y":420,"width":380,"height":902},
		{"id":"c2082de88174bacc","type":"text","text":"# Dancing on Death\n\nVerena tells me that the cemetery is used more like a park; people eat, do yoga on the grass, children play, and even dance. But they don't know that the ground is littered with bones and human bodies. It's a meeting place between life and death.\n\n![Dancing on Death](2026-06-02-dancing-on-death.jpeg)\n","x":1340,"y":720,"width":380,"height":911},
		{"id":"b63995c4444c40b1","type":"text","text":"# Pilgrim of Death\n\nVerena tells me that people go to great lengths to visit certain graves. They sometimes travel from far away. Others come as if they were going to a museum. The cemetery is truly a place rich in activity, a meeting point between life and death. A place of celebration?\n\n![](2026-06-02-pilgrim-of-death.jpeg)\n\n","x":1820,"y":480,"width":380,"height":911},
		{"id":"4b04caf933763e09","type":"text","text":"*List of stories collected during interviews and observations at the Cimetière des Rois.*","x":780,"y":-40,"width":380,"height":85,"color":"3"}
	],
	"edges":[]
}